⚠️ Problem 2: Bad design / mixed responsibilities
If you just use a static field, the class is half object, half global utility.
It becomes confusing — is Counter meant to be instantiated or not?

A Singleton is more intentional:
you’re clearly saying “only one of these can ever exist.” It communicates purpose and avoids misuse.

A Singleton’s getInstance() method lets you:
Create the object lazily (only when first needed), or even swap it out for a mock (for testing).
So it gives you more flexibility and safety.

